            "Doppler shift of your echo (round trip) = 2 × my Doppler.\nWith fixed tuning you hear your echo shifted by this value.",
            "One-way Doppler between the DX and the Moon (Hz).\nIn CFOM the DX transmits on f0 - (this value) and receives on f0 + (this value).",
            "Total shift of the DX signal as you receive it,\nif both stations use fixed tuning on f0 (no correction):\nmy Doppler + DX Doppler.",
            "Frequency on which you must transmit in CFOM (Constant Frequency On the Moon):\nf0 - my Doppler. So your signal reaches the Moon exactly at f0.\nf0 = CFOM frequency set: MHz + kHz (e.g. 144 and 180 = 144.180 MHz).",
            "Frequency on which you must receive in CFOM: f0 + my Doppler.\nIf the DX also works in CFOM, you hear it exactly on this frequency.",
            "Topocentric declination of the Moon seen from your station (degrees):\nheight above the celestial equator. With high (positive) declination\nfrom Europe the Moon stays above the horizon longer and rises higher.",
            "Hour angle of the Moon from your station: negative = east and rising,\n0 = culmination (maximum elevation), positive = descending. 15° = 1 hour.",
