            "THE SKY AS SEEN FROM GRAVES",
            "Moon path over the next 12 h",
            "Four phased arrays cover the southern sky, from 90° to 270° azimuth, in four 45° sectors (D, C, B, A); each sector is divided into 6 steps of 7.5°, illuminated one after another, at the same time in all four sectors. The beam is about 25° wide in elevation: lunar echoes are received well with the Moon between 15° and 40° elevation as seen from GRAVES.",
            "CHRONOLOGICAL RECONSTRUCTION OF THE TRANSMISSIONS · {0} UTC",
