            "Echo possible at this instant",
            "Chooses the budget to check: the one in the EME budget Yagi tab or the one in the EME budget dishes tab (dishes at 432, 902 and 1296 MHz).",
            "Budget",
            "+ {0:F1} dB circular polarization (KA1GT)",
            "not included (circular polarization)",
            "Polarization loss (circular)",
            "{0:F1} dB: circular polarization, typical loss of real feeds (KA1GT)",
            "isolation between the feed ports about 10 dB (KA1GT)",
            "Prime focus",
            "Prime-focus dish (feed in front of the centre of the dish) or offset (feed outside the aperture). With offset the diameter is the projected aperture, i.e. the minor axis, and there is no blockage by the feed and its supports, which in prime focus costs at least 0.5 dB (W2IMU, Crawford Hill TR #18): the typical efficiency rises from 60 to 65%.",
            "Dish type",
            "Projected aperture (minor axis)",
            "no blockage (W2IMU)",
            "typical 65–80%",
            "→ focal length {0:F2} m (parent paraboloid)",
            "offset: D = projected aperture (W2IMU)",
            "The same calculation as the EME budget Yagi, for stations with a dish antenna, at 432, 902 and 1296 MHz, with values stored separately. In each station's tab you choose a prime-focus or offset dish (with offset the diameter is the projected aperture, i.e. the minor axis, and there is no feed blockage: W2IMU) and enter diameter, efficiency (60% on average, 60–80% typical) and f/D ratio; the gain is calculated with the PE1RKI formula, G = 10·log[η·(π·D/λ)²], with dBd (dBi − 2.15) and the −3 dB beamwidth (70·λ/D). The diagram shows the dish with its feed and the complete chain: single- or two-stage preamplifier (up to about 30 dB), feed line, transverter with its transmit output and the cable to the amplifier, with a check of the drive power required by the PA.",
            "1.7 - Eight new languages: Brazilian Portuguese, Thai, Traditional Chinese, Polish, Czech, Romanian, Greek and Hungarian (36 in all), with the manuals and the READMEs; in EME budget Yagi and EME budget dishes, the echo calculation for your own station (I transmit and receive my own echo); prime-focus or offset dish (W2IMU); at 1296 MHz with dishes, the circular polarization loss of real feeds (KA1GT); in Calculation check, the choice between EME budget Yagi and EME budget dishes; formulas of DGRD by frequency written as in an equation editor; manual: Faraday rotation at 1296 MHz according to ITU-R P.531, depolarization at 23 cm (Hagfors) and circular polarization on 23 cm.",
            "1.8 - New Slovak language (37 in total), with the manuals, the README and the licence; one beamwidth throughout the program: 0.93·√(41253/G) for Yagis (Kraus's rule corrected with W4RNL's NEC simulations, as in YA-MS) and 70·λ/D for dishes (IZ0JNY), replacing the unsourced √(32000/G) in DGRD by frequency; manual updated with the new formula and the pointing example; on macOS the launcher starts XQuartz by itself, writes the Mono version to the log and warns if YAEC does not start; README presentation also in Portuguese, Turkish, Czech, Slovak, Chinese, Japanese and Korean; translations corrected in Thai, Romanian, Greek, Brazilian Portuguese, Polish, Czech and Hungarian.",
