            "Example calculation, very approximate.",
            "The setup of the DX stations is reconstructed from what they write in the N0UK chat (144 MHz only): number of antennas, elements and power. The gain is estimated from the number of elements with the DL6WU rule; cables, preamplifier and Tant are typical values. The index only gives a presumed indication of feasibility day by day: compare it with the QSOs you actually make and use it to calibrate the capabilities of your station.",
