            "Geert Stams PA3CSG, \"You worked everybody on 144 MHz EME so try 432 MHz EME\" (0.1 dB ahead of the preamp ≈ 7 K, DL9KR); Peter Blair G3LTF, \"Practical Optimization of 432 MHz and up EME systems using VK3UM's EMECalc\" (Y-factor, measured G/T of the 6 m dish); Doug McArthur VK3UM, EMECalc; Mumford's formula (1961) for wire meshes; cos^q feed (W1GHZ, Microwave Antenna Book).",
            "1.9.5 - EME budget yagi and dishes: cost of 0.1 dB more loss ahead of the preamp (PA3CSG) and new Station test section with G/T on cold sky and the predicted Y-factor on the Sun, Moon, Cas A and ground (G3LTF, VK3UM's EMECalc); EME budget dishes: illumination drop at the edge and dish mesh, with Tant estimated from sky, spillover and mesh, and G3LTF's measured G/T for comparison; new paragraph in the manual; minimum measurable ΔT row with the bandwidth and the integration time τ (Antenna Engineering Handbook, eq. 41-21); DX terrain: SRTM1 horizon around its locator in the My horizon tab, taken into account by common windows, the 24-hour bar, the Sky view and Stations to try (locator of at least 6 characters); antenna SWR in the station test (AEH eq. 41-19); Sun diameter from 0.524° to 0.542° with the Earth–Sun distance; note «YAEC computes, it does not design equipment» in the sources and tips.",
            "Integration time τ",
