            "Antenna SWR",
            "SWR",
            "Standing-wave ratio of the antenna or feed as seen by the preamplifier, for the Y-factor station test. The mismatch reflects a fraction ρ = ((SWR − 1)/(SWR + 1))² of the source noise, which does not reach the receiver: the predicted Y drops (Antenna Engineering Handbook, 4th ed., eq. 41-19). The part ρ·TR of the noise leaving the receiver and coming back reflected is unknown and remains a systematic error.",
            "Antenna SWR {0}:1: ρ = {1}, the Y of Sun, Moon and Cas A drops by the factor (1 − ρ) (AEH eq. 41-19); the reflected receiver noise, ρ·TR, is unknown and remains a systematic error",
            "Faraday rotation can make one of the two directions fail: the second polarization is needed (H and V or XPOL)",
            "polarizations nearly crossed: switch H/V or use circular",
            "H and V (XPOL)",
            "circular",
            "Polarization of your antenna",
            "With a single linear polarization (H only or V only) YAEC flags the times when the contact is at risk: up to 432 MHz when Faraday rotation can make one of the two directions fail (Dpol near ±45°), higher up when the polarizations are nearly crossed. With H and V (or XPOL) the risk drops, with circular there is none.",
            "by band",
            "Polarization of the DX antenna",
